> A bounded batch can genuinely fail

With p=11 and g=2, the default 24-row sample happens never to use the
factor-base prime seven. Its matrix has rank three for four variables modulo
two, so the table is correctly unready. All nonzero targets still have
logarithms; this is a sample-rank failure, not proof of nonexistence. A
separately requested larger batch in the next block produces a verified table,
then reuses it for every nonzero target. There is no silent retry or brute-force
fallback.

Domain checks reject nonprime moduli, zero residues and nongenerators before
trivial-target shortcuts. The p=2 group is handled explicitly without invalid
exponent ranges. Attempts are real finite budgets: zero means no trials, whereas
zero optional allocation/history caps disables those caps. A trivial target one
or g needs no target trial after the group/table checks.

The default sieve cap admits the complete B+1 Boolean positions. The default
matrix cap admits the entire (K+surplus)·K cell request before collection, even
if a smaller attempt budget would collect fewer rows. Both default to one
million. Trace records reserve 1+K logical units per accepted relation or linear
stage, including a failed stage with an empty solution. The one-million-unit
optional history cap is checked before append and returns no partial trace on
error. Excluded are ordinary matrices/working copies, table/output arrays,
scalar/seed metadata, vector capacity and byte/peak RAM. Untraced preparation
ignores that history cap. Counter totals exclude primality/generator validation,
factorization, sieve work, modular-power internals, allocation/copying and final
exponent checks.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/index_calculus_limits.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/index_calculus_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/modular_exponentiation.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto failed = dm::algorithms::index_calculus_prepare_trace(2, 11);
    std::print("Default p=11: accepted {}, rank {} of {}, explicitly rank deficient {}.\n",
               failed.relations.size(), failed.stages.back().rank,
               failed.table.factor_base.size(),
               failed.table.status ==
               dm::algorithms::IndexCalculusStatus::rank_deficient);
    dm::algorithms::IndexCalculusOptions larger;
    larger.relation_surplus = 1000;
    const auto table =
        dm::algorithms::index_calculus_prepare(2, 11, 0x1D2C3B4A59687766ULL,
                                               larger);
    std::print("| reused-table target | recovered exponent | target trials | exponent verified |\n| ---: | " "---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::uint64_t h = 1; h < 11; ++h) {
        const auto q = dm::algorithms::index_calculus_query(table, h);
        if (!q.result.found)
            throw std::runtime_error("reused query failed");
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", h, q.result.x, q.attempts,
                   dm::algorithms::mod_pow(2, q.result.x, 11) == h);
    }
    const auto tiny = dm::algorithms::index_calculus_prepare_trace(2, 5);
    const auto units =
        (tiny.relations.size() + tiny.stages.size()) * (1 +
                                                        tiny.table.factor_base.size());
    dm::algorithms::IndexCalculusOptions exact;
    exact.max_history_entries = units;
    (void) dm::algorithms::index_calculus_prepare_trace(2, 5,
                                                        0x1D2C3B4A59687766ULL,
                                                        exact);
    exact.max_history_entries = units - 1;
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::index_calculus_prepare_trace(
            2, 5, 0x1D2C3B4A59687766ULL, exact);
        throw std::runtime_error("history cap accepted");
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        std::print("Exact {} history units admitted; one-short cap rejected.\n",
                   units);
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::index_calculus(0, 1, 5);
        throw std::runtime_error("zero base accepted");
    } catch (const std::invalid_argument &) {
        std::print("Zero generator rejected even for target one.\n");
    }
    dm::algorithms::index_calculus_preparation_diagram(failed).save_svg(
        "build/index_calculus_limits.svg");
}
```
