> Retain the original asymptotic models without treating them as measurements

For a hypothetical large p, the notation
\(L_p[\alpha,c]=\exp((c+o(1))(\log p)^\alpha(\log\log p)^{1-\alpha})\) describes
an asymptotic form. The classical smoothness tradeoff balances a larger factor
base and denser linear algebra against fewer rejected relation trials. Under the
associated parameter choices and smoothness assumptions, classical
index-calculus analyses lead to an L[1/2,c] form; the finite capped batch
implemented here does not establish that asymptotic runtime.

The original eight 30-to-240-bit formula points use the illustrative constant
c=√2. We preserve those values and the square-root comparison, evaluating their
logarithms directly without exponentiating huge costs:

$$
\log_{10}L_{model}=\frac{c\sqrt{\log p\log\log p}}{\log 10},\qquad
\log_{10}\sqrt p=\frac{\log p}{2\log10}.
$$
\alttext(The two plotted formula values are computed directly as decimal logarithms, without a runtime experiment.)

These curves omit hidden constants and lower-order terms. Bit sizes above 64 are
outside this implementation's input type. Their crossing is not an empirical
crossover, a proof of this code's speed or a security/key-size recommendation.
No unrelated dataset is needed for the arithmetic and relation controls.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/index_calculus_models.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/index_calculus_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/modular_exponentiation.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto models =
        dm::algorithms::index_calculus_cost_models({30, 60, 90, 120, 150, 180,
                                                    210, 240});
    std::vector<double> bits, index, generic;
    std::print("| hypothetical bits | illustrative L-model log10 | square-root model log10 |\n| ---: | ---: " "| ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &m : models) {
        std::print("| {} | {:.2f} | {:.2f} |\n", m.bits, m.index_log10,
                   m.generic_log10);
        bits.push_back(m.bits);
        index.push_back(m.index_log10);
        generic.push_back(m.generic_log10);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(bits, index, "L model", {124, 58, 237}, 2).line(bits, generic,
                                                           "sqrt model",
                                                           {220, 38, 38}, 2).title("Illustrative asymptotic formulas, not measured work").x_label("hypothetical bits of p (above 64 exceeds API)").y_label("log10 formula value").y_limits(0, 43).save_svg("build/index_calculus_models.svg");
}
```
